    nine species from the SIMPLE Forest Animals pack, named by the owner on 2026-09-26. FA1 is art
    and roster only, so each carries the fields that exist today - pace, pool, wander, rest,
    revenge, attack - and the four FA1 adds: formCount (the deer's doe and stag, the moose's cow and
    bull, derived from the pawn's seed and never saved), bodySizePerMille (against a colonist's
    1,000; design 65's prey limit and design 64's herd read it), and meatYield and hideYield, which
    nothing reads until hunting (cooking's K3) and which are here because the owner asked for the
    stats now (answer 15).

    Every one is TraverseMode.Animal: no ladder, no door, no water - the raccoon too, so that a
    closed door keeps a store raid out (plan section 1). The revenge numbers are FA1's, the hog's
    rule for the animals that stand and fight and nought for the ones that run; design 64's
    temperament numbers, with their x3 in melee, replace them in FA2. Attacks are sized from design
    64's table against the hog's 6 every 150 ticks. bodyLengthMm is life length x the colonists'
    draw factor of about 1.42 (design 66 section 5), for presentation only. Every number is
    INVENTED unless it says otherwise, and a playtest number.
