  <!--
    The bandit (design 33 section 1): a person under the Hostile faction, debug-spawned, armed,
    hunting the nearest reachable colonist who is standing. Hostility comes from the kind, so no
    pawn carries a saved field for it (section 3). A person species, rolled as a colonist is,
    and dressed as a bandit on top of that: welding helmet, red vest, black trousers (design 42).
    Its needs do not tick (Pawn.NeedsTick), so the needs fields below are the type's defaults and
    unread.
  -->
  <PawnKindDef>
    <defName>PawnKind_Bandit</defName>
    <species>Species_Person</species>
    <faction>Hostile</faction>
    <!-- Armed from the moment it arrives (design 33 section 1), with one of these, dealt per
         bandit by a hash of the pawn rather than a draw (design 42 section 3). A crowbar or a bat,
         never a blade (owner, 2026-09-24: "not swords - not their style"). -->
    <weapons>
      <li>Item_Crowbar</li>
      <li>Item_Bat</li>
    </weapons>
    <!-- A person who does not open the colony's doors (design 33 section 16; owner, 2026-09-24:
         "do what you recommend"). Ladders, stairs, the hop and the wade as a colonist, but a
         closed door is a wall: with the colonists behind one, it breaks the door down. -->
    <traverseMode>Bandit</traverseMode>
    <!-- What it came for, once nobody is left standing to fight and nothing is left to break
         (design 33 section 17; owner, 2026-09-24: "thieve items or kidnap people depending on
         their motivation ... for now - thieve items"). Loot carries the nearest stack off the
         board; Kidnap is the seam and does exactly what Loot does today. -->
    <motive>Loot</motive>
  </PawnKindDef>

  <!--
    The gunman (design 55 section 8): the bandit with a pistol. Its own kind rather than a bandit
    handed a weapon, so a raid mix can name it and a storyteller can draw it; everything else is
    the bandit's - a person, Hostile, the same traverse mode and motive, and the same outfit,
    because PawnOutfits keys on a hostile person rather than on the kind. The pistol is the only
    row in its table, so every gunman carries one.
  -->
  <PawnKindDef>
    <defName>PawnKind_Gunman</defName>
    <species>Species_Person</species>
    <faction>Hostile</faction>
    <weapons>
      <li>Item_Pistol</li>
    </weapons>
    <traverseMode>Bandit</traverseMode>
    <motive>Loot</motive>
  </PawnKindDef>

